%description:
Tests that the delayed ACK counts the bytes against RMSS, the MSS of the
receiver (RFC 9293 SHLD-19: "at least every second full-sized segment or
2*RMSS bytes of new data"). The server sends no MSS option, so its RMSS is
the default 536, and the client sends segments of 536 bytes, shorter than
the send MSS of the server (1024). The server acknowledges the two segments
of 1072 bytes at once, not at the delayed ACK timeout.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 1072"
*.cli_tcp.increasedIWEnabled = true # two segments at once
*.srv_tcp.sendMssOption = false

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[1.001 A003] A.1000 > B.2000: A 1:537(536) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.001 A004] A.1000 > B.2000: A 537:1073(536) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.003 B002] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 1073 win 16384 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
